  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「クサヨシ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AF%E3%82%B5%E3%83%A8%E3%82%B7",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 108387397,
      "text": "クサヨシ は、イネ科クサヨシ属の多年草である。背が高くなる草で、1.5mを越える物もある。和名は、ヨシに似て茎が柔らかいことからついた名前。リードカナリーグラスとも呼ばれる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Phalaris arundinacea」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phalaris_arundinacea",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1371184521,
      "text": "Phalaris arundinacea, or reed canary grass, is a tall, perennial grass that commonly forms extensive single-species stands along the margins of lakes and streams and in wet open areas, with a wide distribution in Europe, Asia, northern Africa and North America. Other common names for the plant include gardener's-garters and ribbon grass in English, alpiste roseau in French, Rohrglanzgras in German, kusa-yoshi in Japanese, caniço-malhado in Portuguese, and hierba cinta and pasto cinto in Spanish."
    }
  },
